  "body": "The SVG2 spec defines that [the HTML audio/video/iframe/canvas elements should work in SVG](https://svgwg.org/svg2-draft/embedded.html#HTMLElements).  That's a little bit inconvenient in SVG's XML serialization, as you have to include another namespace, but it's actually _impossible_ currently in embedded SVG, as you don't use namespaces manually at all.\n\nThe parser, when it switches into parsing SVG, should have a list of elements that are put into the HTML namespace automatically.  At minimum, this should be audio/video/iframe/canvas, + picture.  Child elements should also automatically be in the HTML namespace (unless you hit an <svg> subtree, obviously).\n",
